00:55:12,000 --> 00:55:18,000
Safe House is a 2012 American action thriller film directed by Daniel Espinosa, written
by David Guggenheim, and starring Denzel Washington and Ryan Reynolds.

13
00:59:48,000 --> 00:59:54,000
The film follows Matt Weston (Reynolds), a CIA officer on a low-level posting in Cape Town, South Africa, who is in charge of a safe
house where the CIA is interrogating Tobin Frost (Washington), a veteran operative accused of betraying the agency.

14
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
When the safe house is attacked by mercenaries,
Weston flees with Frost in his charge.

15
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:06,000
As the team of killers, who seem to be one step ahead of the pair, track
them throughout Cape Town, Weston wonders who to trust.

16
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:42,000
Vera Farmiga, Brendan Gleeson, Sam Shepard, Rubén Blades,
Nora Arnezeder and Robert Patrick co-star.

17
01:18:12,000 --> 01:18:18,000
Safe House was Espinosa's first English-language film.

18
01:22:48,000 --> 01:22:54,000
Filming took place on location in Cape Town.

19
01:27:24,000 --> 01:27:30,000
The film premiered in New York City on February
7, 2012, and was released in U.S.

20
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:06,000
theaters on February 10, 2012, by Universal Pictures.

21
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
The film earned mixed reviews, with praise for Washington and Reynolds' performances, but
negative criticisms for the screenplay and the editing of the action scenes.

22
01:41:12,000 --> 01:41:18,000
Nevertheless, the film was a commercial success, earning $208
million worldwide against an $85 million budget.

23
01:45:48,000 --> 01:45:54,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, central intelligence
agency (cia), microchip, betrayal, on the run.

24
01:50:24,000 --> 01:50:30,000
The tone is intense.
